WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.246
Business onboarding brings together accounts,

2
00:00:08.246 --> 00:00:10.266
ACH, wires and entitlements.

3
00:00:10.266 --> 00:00:13.512
The work crosses systems, teams and controls.

4
00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:16.220
Follow one onboarding request.

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.567
A logistics company, setting up treasury services.

6
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.908
The relationship manager opens it.

7
00:00:22.908 --> 00:00:26.642
It moves through KYC, treasury ops and core banking.

8
00:00:26.642 --> 00:00:29.514
Then it comes back for more information,

9
00:00:29.514 --> 00:00:32.099
and the same form is keyed in again.

10
00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:35.976
At ACH limit approval, it waits six days in one queue.

11
00:00:36.976 --> 00:00:38.206
Business day eleven.

12
00:00:38.206 --> 00:00:40.112
Entitlements are still pending.

13
00:00:42.512 --> 00:00:46.024
Local reports show completed tasks and open work.

14
00:00:46.024 --> 00:00:48.891
End-to-end activation time is not shown.

15
00:00:51.691 --> 00:00:54.891
Completed tasks. An unfinished customer journey.

16
00:00:56.191 --> 00:00:58.259
The delay may sit between the steps.

17
00:00:58.259 --> 00:01:01.247
Separate records make the whole journey hard to see.

18
00:01:01.947 --> 00:01:05.407
RE-ViVE connects the operational records your bank already

19
00:01:05.407 --> 00:01:08.987
keeps, and reconstructs how the request actually progressed.

20
00:01:09.587 --> 00:01:13.468
See where time accumulated, and what remains open today.

21
00:01:13.468 --> 00:01:15.616
Investigate the approval queue.

22
00:01:15.616 --> 00:01:18.388
Confirm ownership of pending user setup.

23
00:01:18.388 --> 00:01:20.468
Source access stays read-only.

24
00:01:20.468 --> 00:01:22.685
Required checks remain in place.

25
00:01:23.585 --> 00:01:26.273
Opening the relationship is one milestone.

26
00:01:26.273 --> 00:01:28.961
Getting the customer operating is another.

27
00:01:30.461 --> 00:01:32.181
Request a banking walkthrough.

28
00:01:32.181 --> 00:01:35.219
See how one customer journey connects across systems,

29
00:01:35.219 --> 00:01:37.053
and how to trace where it waits.